# Drafted by Gemini (R21 crowd), edited.

~ search
Narrator: Paper ribbons snap overhead and hot mutton grease thickens the air while the townsfolk whirl in an endless, blister-footed reel. Painted grins flash past you in the bonfire glare, too wide and too bright to ever rest.
* Spend an hour searching the crowd for friends in costume -> hour
* Ask a dancer who will talk -> ask_dancer
* Leave -> END

~ ask_dancer
Narrator: You catch a spinning villager by her ribboned sleeve, though her heels never stop their frantic drumming on the cobbles.
Narrator: Keep step, darlings, before the music catches you standing still! Every one of Chuckles's costumed troupe lurks right beside the game booth that matches its dress, so play a round and you'll spot its twin!
-> search

~ hour
time +60
set fd_searched += 1
Narrator: For a whole hour you shoulder through sticky elbows, spilled cider, and a hundred painted faces that all laugh on the same shrill beat.
-> tiers

~ tiers
* [if not flag.found_flag] [Investigation DC 5] Look for the flag-carriers -> t_flag | miss
* [if not flag.found_bear] [Investigation DC 10] Look for a horned bear -> t_bear | miss
* [if not flag.found_hive] [Investigation DC 14] Look for a queen bee's hive -> t_hive | miss
* [if not flag.found_hut] [Investigation DC 16] Look for a house on chicken legs -> t_hut | miss
* [if not flag.found_bell] [Investigation DC 18] Look for a chiming bell -> t_bell | miss
* [if not flag.found_knight] [Investigation DC 20] Look for a knight with a book -> t_knight | miss
* [if not flag.found_stork] [Investigation DC 22] Look for a stilted stork -> t_stork | miss
* Stop searching -> END

~ t_flag
set found_flag
Narrator: Through a gap in the bonfire smoke, you spot twin standards snapping near the red-ribboned puppet theater.
-> tiers

~ t_bear
set found_bear
Narrator: Over the heads of the reel, a hulking horned bear costume sways beside the arm-wrestling table in the east.
-> tiers

~ t_hive
set found_hive
Narrator: A faint droning carries over the fiddles from the north-west, where a towering wicker hive bobs near the dart cabinets.
-> tiers

~ t_hut
set found_hut
Narrator: Down in the south-west lane, a crooked little manor on scaly chicken legs struts and hops beside the drinking stall.
-> tiers

~ t_bell
set found_bell
Narrator: A brassy chime rings out from the north, where a walking bell costume gleams beside the shell game.
-> tiers

~ t_knight
set found_knight
Narrator: Near the riddle stall in the north-east, a tin-plated knight clutches a singing tome to his chest.
-> tiers

~ t_stork
set found_stork
Narrator: High above the lanterns in the west, a long-beaked stork teeters on tall stilts beside the thunder of the drummers.
-> tiers

~ miss
Narrator: Too many faces press around you, all of them grinning the same wet, breathless grin until your eyes ache.
-> tiers

~ shove
Narrator: A surging ring of revellers catches you by the shoulders and shoves you along in a stink of sour ale and scorched sugar.
Narrator: Dance till your soles peel right off the bone, sweethearts, for the clock is broke and morning's never coming home!
ambrose_quill [smile]: Stuff another hot pie down your gullet before your ribs split! Our Lord on the maypole loves a merry, bursting belly!
old_rusty [smile]: Round and round the cobbles go, drop your bones and point your toe, stop for breath and down you go!
-> END

~ calliope
Narrator: Half-hidden behind a tent flap sits a brass calliope wagon with a loose panel concealing a moon-shaped button. Scratched into the paint beside it, in your own unmistakable handwriting, are the words: 'the goat lies'.
* Press the button -> press
* Leave it alone -> END

~ press
Narrator: The steam pipes wheeze out a warped, weeping mockery of your own cradle song as smoke boils across your sight. Through the haze rises a colossal goat skull crowned in mire, and a chorus of throats screaming to butcher it upon the stone.
set apocalypse_calliope
-> END

~ joker
Narrator: Pinned to a splintered stall post with a rusty nail is a gleaming joker card, its price tag marked with a sideways figure eight for infinity tickets. At your feet, your own shadow stretches across the dirt, its dark fingers twitching toward the card.
* Let the shadow take it -> take
* Leave it -> END

~ take
Narrator: Your shadow plucks the card free, and a dry paper chuckle whispers against your palm, boasting of impossible luck if only you wager a whole realm of the dead.
give wild_joker_card
set liberation_wild_joker
-> END
